#: krusader/Dialogs/krmaskchoice.cpp:101
msgid ""
"A predefined selection is a file-mask which you use often.\n"
"Some examples are: \"*.c, *.h\", \"*.c, *.o\", etc.\n"
"You can add these masks to the list by typing them and pressing the Add button.\n"
"Delete removes a predefined selection and Clear removes all of them.\n"
"Notice that the line in which you edit the mask has it's own history, you can scroll it, if needed."
msgstr ""
"En vörinstellt Köör is en Dateimuster, dat Du faken bruukst.\n"
"Bispelen sünd \"*.c, *.h\", \"*.c, *.o\" usw.\n"
"Du kannst disse Mustern de List tofögen, wenn Du dat Muster ingiffst un op \"Tofögen\" klickst.\n"
"\"Wegdoon\" deit een vörinstellt Muster weg, \"Leddig maken\" deit all Mustern weg.\n"
"Beacht bitte, de Reeg, binnen de Du dat Muster bewerken deist, hett ehr egen Vörgeschicht. Du kannst dor binnen rop un daal rullen."

